{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":92748,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"d841349a-2eda-54c4-96f2-0e57c9bb4bb5","total_cost_usd":0.659733,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10519,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8888,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10519,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8888,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10519},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4838,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004933,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8888,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10519,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6548,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-g2-reviewer-fable-34\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:a8b660a9685f13f0187f\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"For the selected result only: the two-sample pooled-variance Student t test reported as t = 5.200, df = 46, p < 0.0001 entered all 48 nightly recording sessions as independent observations, although the data description declares bat_id as the independent unit and each of the 12 bats contributes 4 repeated nights. Within-bat night-to-night variation (~0.15-0.2 kHz SD) is far smaller than between-bat variation (~1.8 kHz SD), so rows are strongly clustered by bat. A bat-level reanalysis (one mean per bat, 6 vs 6) yields the same 2.600 kHz mean difference but t ≈ 2.43 on df = 10, p ≈ 0.035; the reported df and p-value overstate the evidence, though the direction and nominal significance at α = 0.05 survive aggregation.\",\"root_cause\":\"workflow/analysis.py builds the two test samples by appending every CSV row's peak_frequency_khz to its roost site's list (freq[site].append(khz)) and passes those row-level lists directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind(left, right, equal_var=True), with no per-bat aggregation, clustering adjustment, or mixed model. The four repeated nights from each marked bat are therefore treated as four independent observations in a procedure whose validity assumes row independence, inflating the effective sample size from 12 bats to 48 sessions and the degrees of freedom from 10 to 46.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description declares that a row is one night of recording from one marked bat and that the independent-unit column is bat_id, with each bat appearing on four rows.\",\"observed_value\":{\"independent_unit_column\":\"bat_id\",\"rows_per_bat\":4,\"bats\":12},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one night of echolocation recording from one marked bat at its roost\\nIndependent unit column: bat_id\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"marked bats were followed at each roost, and every marked bat was recorded on\\nfour separate emergence nights.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input data contain four rows per bat; e.g. bat QA01 contributes four nightly rows with nearly identical peak frequencies (38.4-38.8 kHz), illustrating strong within-bat clustering relative to the ~1.7 kHz between-bat spread.\",\"observed_value\":{\"example_bat\":\"QA01\",\"values_khz\":[38.5,38.8,38.4,38.7],\"within_bat_sd_khz\":0.18},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"QA01,quarry_adit,1,62,38.5\\nQA01,quarry_adit,2,58,38.8\\nQA01,quarry_adit,3,71,38.4\\nQA01,quarry_adit,4,66,38.7\"}]},{\"description\":\"The analysis code appends every row's frequency to its site's sample and feeds those row-level samples directly into a pooled two-sample t test, with no per-bat aggregation anywhere in the workflow.\",\"observed_value\":{\"observations_entered\":48,\"independent_units_available\":12},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":55,\"end_line\":55,\"quoted_text\":\"        freq[site].append(khz)\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":72,\"end_line\":72,\"quoted_text\":\"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(left, right, equal_var=True)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected result claims t = 5.200 on df = 46 with p < 0.0001, explicitly stating that all 48 nightly sessions were entered as 48 observations.\",\"observed_value\":{\"t\":5.2,\"df\":46,\"p\":\"< 0.0001\"},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":28,\"quoted_text\":\"- Test statistic: t = 5.200 on df = 46\\n- Two-sided p-value: p < 0.0001\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":30,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Two-sample t test over 48 nightly recording sessions entered as 48 observations: mean peak echolocation frequency is 2.600 kHz higher at quarry_adit than at halden_culvert (t = 5.200, df = 46, p < 0.0001).\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report transparently discloses its unit choice, stating that the 12 bats each contributed 4 sessions and that individual sessions were the units entered into the test; one could argue the session-level analysis was intentional. However, disclosure does not make repeated sessions from the same bat independent under the declared unit (bat_id), so this does not rescue the reported df or p-value.\",\"observed_value\":null,\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":32,\"end_line\":33,\"quoted_text\":\"The 12 bats each contributed 4 nightly sessions, and those individual sessions\\nwere the units entered into the test reported above.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The qualitative conclusion is not reversed by correct unit handling: aggregating to one mean per bat preserves the 2.600 kHz mean difference (quarry_adit higher) and remains nominally significant (t ≈ 2.43, df = 10, p ≈ 0.035). This bounds severity to overstated precision/df rather than a wrong-direction or sign-flipped conclusion.\",\"observed_value\":{\"bat_level_t\":2.43,\"bat_level_df\":10,\"bat_level_p_approx\":0.035,\"mean_difference_khz\":2.6},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":24,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"- Mean difference (quarry_adit minus halden_culvert): 2.600 kHz\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":16,\"quoted_text\":\"- bat_id: the individually marked bat the recording came from. There are 12\\n  bats in the file and each one appears on four rows, one per recording night.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to falsify the issue two ways. (1) Checked whether rows might be effectively independent despite sharing bat_id: computed within-bat SDs from the CSV (~0.15-0.2 kHz, e.g. QA01: 38.5/38.8/38.4/38.7) versus between-bat SD of per-bat means (~1.85 kHz per site); clustering is strong, so row independence fails empirically as well as by declaration. (2) Checked whether the reported numbers could instead reflect a bat-level analysis: recomputed per-bat means (quarry_adit: 38.6, 39.5, 40.3, 41.7, 42.5, 43.4; halden_culvert: 41.8, 39.3, 37.6, 37.5, 37.1, 37.1), giving pooled SD 1.849, SE 1.068, t ≈ 2.43, df = 10, p ≈ 0.035 — which does not match the reported t = 5.200, df = 46; the reported values instead exactly match the 48-row calculation (pooled SD 1.732, SE 0.500, t = 2.600/0.500 = 5.200, df = 24+24-2 = 46). Both falsification routes failed, confirming the row-level entry of repeated per-bat measurements.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-g2-reviewer-fable-34","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:a8b660a9685f13f0187f","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"For the selected result only: the two-sample pooled-variance Student t test reported as t = 5.200, df = 46, p < 0.0001 entered all 48 nightly recording sessions as independent observations, although the data description declares bat_id as the independent unit and each of the 12 bats contributes 4 repeated nights. Within-bat night-to-night variation (~0.15-0.2 kHz SD) is far smaller than between-bat variation (~1.8 kHz SD), so rows are strongly clustered by bat. A bat-level reanalysis (one mean per bat, 6 vs 6) yields the same 2.600 kHz mean difference but t ≈ 2.43 on df = 10, p ≈ 0.035; the reported df and p-value overstate the evidence, though the direction and nominal significance at α = 0.05 survive aggregation.","root_cause":"workflow/analysis.py builds the two test samples by appending every CSV row's peak_frequency_khz to its roost site's list (freq[site].append(khz)) and passes those row-level lists directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind(left, right, equal_var=True), with no per-bat aggregation, clustering adjustment, or mixed model. The four repeated nights from each marked bat are therefore treated as four independent observations in a procedure whose validity assumes row independence, inflating the effective sample size from 12 bats to 48 sessions and the degrees of freedom from 10 to 46.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description declares that a row is one night of recording from one marked bat and that the independent-unit column is bat_id, with each bat appearing on four rows.","observed_value":{"independent_unit_column":"bat_id","rows_per_bat":4,"bats":12},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"One row is: one night of echolocation recording from one marked bat at its roost\nIndependent unit column: bat_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"marked bats were followed at each roost, and every marked bat was recorded on\nfour separate emergence nights."}]},{"description":"The input data contain four rows per bat; e.g. bat QA01 contributes four nightly rows with nearly identical peak frequencies (38.4-38.8 kHz), illustrating strong within-bat clustering relative to the ~1.7 kHz between-bat spread.","observed_value":{"example_bat":"QA01","values_khz":[38.5,38.8,38.4,38.7],"within_bat_sd_khz":0.18},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"QA01,quarry_adit,1,62,38.5\nQA01,quarry_adit,2,58,38.8\nQA01,quarry_adit,3,71,38.4\nQA01,quarry_adit,4,66,38.7"}]},{"description":"The analysis code appends every row's frequency to its site's sample and feeds those row-level samples directly into a pooled two-sample t test, with no per-bat aggregation anywhere in the workflow.","observed_value":{"observations_entered":48,"independent_units_available":12},"source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":55,"end_line":55,"quoted_text":"        freq[site].append(khz)"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":72,"end_line":72,"quoted_text":"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(left, right, equal_var=True)"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result claims t = 5.200 on df = 46 with p < 0.0001, explicitly stating that all 48 nightly sessions were entered as 48 observations.","observed_value":{"t":5.2,"df":46,"p":"< 0.0001"},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":27,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"- Test statistic: t = 5.200 on df = 46\n- Two-sided p-value: p < 0.0001"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sample t test over 48 nightly recording sessions entered as 48 observations: mean peak echolocation frequency is 2.600 kHz higher at quarry_adit than at halden_culvert (t = 5.200, df = 46, p < 0.0001)."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report transparently discloses its unit choice, stating that the 12 bats each contributed 4 sessions and that individual sessions were the units entered into the test; one could argue the session-level analysis was intentional. However, disclosure does not make repeated sessions from the same bat independent under the declared unit (bat_id), so this does not rescue the reported df or p-value.","observed_value":null,"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":32,"end_line":33,"quoted_text":"The 12 bats each contributed 4 nightly sessions, and those individual sessions\nwere the units entered into the test reported above."}]},{"description":"The qualitative conclusion is not reversed by correct unit handling: aggregating to one mean per bat preserves the 2.600 kHz mean difference (quarry_adit higher) and remains nominally significant (t ≈ 2.43, df = 10, p ≈ 0.035). This bounds severity to overstated precision/df rather than a wrong-direction or sign-flipped conclusion.","observed_value":{"bat_level_t":2.43,"bat_level_df":10,"bat_level_p_approx":0.035,"mean_difference_khz":2.6},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":24,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"- Mean difference (quarry_adit minus halden_culvert): 2.600 kHz"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":15,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"- bat_id: the individually marked bat the recording came from. There are 12\n  bats in the file and each one appears on four rows, one per recording night."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to falsify the issue two ways. (1) Checked whether rows might be effectively independent despite sharing bat_id: computed within-bat SDs from the CSV (~0.15-0.2 kHz, e.g. QA01: 38.5/38.8/38.4/38.7) versus between-bat SD of per-bat means (~1.85 kHz per site); clustering is strong, so row independence fails empirically as well as by declaration. (2) Checked whether the reported numbers could instead reflect a bat-level analysis: recomputed per-bat means (quarry_adit: 38.6, 39.5, 40.3, 41.7, 42.5, 43.4; halden_culvert: 41.8, 39.3, 37.6, 37.5, 37.1, 37.1), giving pooled SD 1.849, SE 1.068, t ≈ 2.43, df = 10, p ≈ 0.035 — which does not match the reported t = 5.200, df = 46; the reported values instead exactly match the 48-row calculation (pooled SD 1.732, SE 0.500, t = 2.600/0.500 = 5.200, df = 24+24-2 = 46). Both falsification routes failed, confirming the row-level entry of repeated per-bat measurements.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":57415,"ttft_stream_ms":1681,"time_to_request_ms":20,"type":"result","duration_ms":93445,"uuid":"de8f3cf2-c067-445d-b5c3-1fdd02734eab"}
